      "math_academy_id": "e-2149",
      "problem": "An object is assembled as shown below. Given that each small cube represents one cubic unit, what is the volume of the object?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14132963/assets/5304eed09b6d029958fbfcce95001c79a8a9dbdd91e7c8ae6eefa7d54db61a75.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The figure consists of two layers:\n\n- The bottom layer consists of $4$ cubes.\n\n- The top layer consists of $1$ cube.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14132963/assets/4c6372a05b21e7aa9f26717fdbb2cfe47e17d2d17215e9b7411e876b0e6473f5.png)\n\nTherefore, the volume is $4+1=5$ cubic units.",
